---
import ContactForm from '@components/ContactForm.astro'
import { SitePage } from '@data/analyticsCaller'
import Grid from '@components/Grid.astro'
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro'
import CaseStudySectionText from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudySectionText.astro'
import CaseStudyResults from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudyResults.astro'
import CaseStudyHeader from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudyHeader.astro'
import CaseStudyToggleButton from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudyToggleButton.astro'
import CaseStudyMetaData from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudyMetaData.astro'
import CaseStudyShout from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudyShout.astro'
import CaseStudyNav from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudyNav.astro'
import CaseStudyImages from '@components/case-studies/case-study/CaseStudyImages.astro'
import { getCaseStudyNav } from '@data/caseStudies'

import hero from '@assets/case-studies/sonata-ai/hero.webp'
import squareOne from '@assets/case-studies/sonata-ai/squareOne.svg'
import squareTwo from '@assets/case-studies/sonata-ai/squareTwo.webp'
import wideOne from '@assets/case-studies/sonata-ai/wideOne.webp'
import wideTwo from '@assets/case-studies/sonata-ai/wideTwo.webp'

const { previous, next } = getCaseStudyNav('ai-risk-calculator')
---

<Layout
  title="AI Risk Calculator Case Study"
  description="Pixel Agency built a custom AI-powered Risk Tool, a CatBoost prediction model that estimates risk from early design inputs, giving architects and designers an instant read at the point decisions are made and positioning the client as the brand that helps them see the problem before it becomes one."
>
  <article id="case-study-page">
    <CaseStudyHeader>
      <span slot="title">AI Risk Calculator</span>
      <span slot="industry">Manufacturing</span>
      <span slot="services">AI</span>
      <span slot="duration">1 month</span>
    </CaseStudyHeader>

    <CaseStudyToggleButton />

    <!-- Single shell: all images + summary (left pane) / all case study text (right pane) -->
    <section class="pb-12 lg:pb-18">
      <Grid>
        <div id="case-study-shell" class="case-study-shell col-span-full">
          <div class="case-study-left-pane min-w-0 overflow-hidden">
            <CaseStudyImages
              heroImage={{ src: hero }}
              summary="How Pixel Agency built a custom AI-powered Risk Tool, giving architects and designers an instant read on whether a space is heading for a problem and putting the client in the conversation early."
              squareImages={[{ src: squareOne }, { src: squareTwo }]}
              wideImages={[{ src: wideOne }, { src: wideTwo }]}
            />
          </div>

          <div class="case-study-right-pane min-w-0">
            <CaseStudyShout> Helping architects spot risks before the design is locked in. </CaseStudyShout>

            <CaseStudySectionText title="The client" noTopMargin={true}>
              <p>
                The client is a leading Australian manufacturer of products designed for commercial fit-outs, offices,
                education spaces, and interiors where product performance matters. The client sells through architects,
                designers, and specifiers, the people who shape a space long before ground is broken in its
                construction. Getting the client's product specified means being part of the conversation early, when
                risks are still questions rather than problems.
              </p><br />
              <p>
                We cannot name the client, or the problem the tool resolves here as they see the calculator as a genuine
                differentiator from their competition. They're planning to surprise the market with this release
                shortly, and want to maintain that competitive advantage until launch.
              </p>
            </CaseStudySectionText>

            <CaseStudySectionText title="The problem">
              <p>
                Performance risk is one of those things that's hard to see until it's too late. A building can look
                right on a plan and still perform poorly once it's built and in use. Architects and designers don't
                always have an easy way to assess the performance risk of a space at the moment they're making the
                decisions that drive it: size, materials, etc. By the time the building is in use, the problem (and the
                cost of fixing it) is locked in.
              </p><br />
              <p>
                The client's marketing team saw an opportunity in that gap. If the client could give architects and
                designers a quick, credible way to assess risks early, the client would stop being just a product to
                specify and start being a useful tool in the design process itself. The challenge was turning that idea
                into something real, technically credible, and trusted by a professional audience.
              </p>
            </CaseStudySectionText>

            <CaseStudySectionText title="The approach">
              <p>
                The client brought the idea to us as a differentiator they wanted to validate. Our job was to take the
                concept from "this could work" to "this does work" by building a working prototype that proved out the
                technical approach and gave the client something tangible to show stakeholders. We started by working
                with the client to define the inputs an architect would actually have at the early design stage, the
                outputs that would be useful at that moment, and the level of confidence the tool needed to project to
                be credible to a professional audience.
              </p><br />
              <p>
                From there we designed the system around a custom AI prediction model: a CatBoost gradient boosting
                model trained on the relationship between building characteristics and risk outcomes. CatBoost was
                chosen because it handles the structured, tabular nature of the design inputs well, performs strongly on
                smaller training datasets, and produces calibrated confidence scores rather than the black-box guesses
                you sometimes get from off-the-shelf AI.
              </p>
            </CaseStudySectionText>

            <CaseStudySectionText title="The solution">
              <p>
                The Risk Tool is built as a self-contained, client-branded application that is designed to embed cleanly
                inside the client website. The architecture is deliberately lightweight: a FastAPI and Pydantic backend
                serving the trained CatBoost model, a client-branded front end for architects and designers, and a
                single dedicated server hosting the model and API. No third-party AI services in the loop, no data
                leaving the client's environment unnecessarily, and full control over the model and its training.
              </p><br />
              <p>
                A user steps through a short, considered set of inputs and the model returns a risk band (Low, Medium,
                or High), a confidence score, and the factors that contributed most to the result, so the answer isn't
                just a number but a starting point for a design conversation. Client products are surfaced as part of
                the response where appropriate, putting the brand in front of architects at the exact moment they're
                thinking about how to bring the risk down.
              </p>
            </CaseStudySectionText>

            <CaseStudySectionText title="The results">
              <p>
                The tool is currently in pre-launch, with a working demonstration validated end-to-end and the model
                trained on representative scenarios:
              </p>
              <CaseStudyResults
                results={[
                  {
                    title: 'A working AI tool',
                    description:
                      'demonstrated end-to-end with the trained CatBoost model returning calibrated risk bands, confidence scores, and contributing factors',
                    backgroundColour: 'pixel-solar'
                  },
                  {
                    title: 'A custom architecture',
                    description:
                      'that gives the client full control over the model, the data, and the training process, with no dependence on third-party AI services',
                    backgroundColour: 'pixel-celestial'
                  },
                  {
                    title: 'A client-branded experience',
                    description:
                      'designed to embed inside the client website, ready to drop into the live site with no disruption',
                    backgroundColour: 'pixel-rosy'
                  }
                ]}
              />

              <div class="mt-6 lg:mt-12"></div>

              <CaseStudyShout>
                Problems are cheap to fix before the building is built. After that, they're not. AI gives us the power
                to see the risk before it's a problem.
              </CaseStudyShout>
            </CaseStudySectionText>

            <CaseStudyMetaData
              client={{ name: 'Redacted', url: 'https://www.pixelagency.com.au/' }}
              industry={['Manufacturing']}
              serviceNames={['Discovery + direction', 'Design', 'Development', 'AI']}
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </Grid>
    </section>

    {/* Navigation section */}
    <CaseStudyNav previousCaseStudy={previous} nextCaseStudy={next} />

    <ContactForm
      title="Discuss a similar challenge"
      displayDescription={false}
      caller={SitePage.CASE_STUDIES_AI_RISK_CALCULATOR}
    />
  </article>

  <style>
    #case-study-page {
      --case-study-border: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-black) 8%, transparent);
      --case-study-placeholder: var(--color-pixel-placeholder-grey);
    }

    @media (max-width: 1023px) {
      .case-study-shell {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0;
        overflow: clip;
      }

      .case-study-left-pane {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        width: 100%;
        max-height: 5000px;
        opacity: 1;
        transform: translateX(0);
        transition:
          width 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
          max-height 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
          opacity 240ms ease,
          transform 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
        will-change: width, max-height, opacity, transform;
      }

      #case-study-page[data-panel-state='open'] .case-study-left-pane {
        width: 0;
        max-height: 0;
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateX(-2rem);
        pointer-events: none;
      }

      .case-study-right-pane {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        width: 0;
        max-height: 0;
        opacity: 0;
        overflow: clip;
        transform: translateX(2rem);
        transition:
          width 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
          max-height 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
          opacity 260ms ease,
          transform 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
        will-change: width, max-height, opacity, transform;
      }

      #case-study-page[data-panel-state='open'] .case-study-right-pane {
        width: 100%;
        max-height: 5000px;
        opacity: 1;
        transform: translateX(0);
        pointer-events: auto;
      }
    }

    @media (min-width: 1024px) {
      .case-study-shell {
        display: flex;
        gap: 0;
        transition: gap 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
      }

      #case-study-page[data-panel-state='open'] .case-study-shell {
        gap: 1.25rem;
      }

      .case-study-left-pane,
      .case-study-right-pane {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        transition:
          width 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
          max-height 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
          opacity 260ms ease,
          transform 420ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
        will-change: width, max-height, opacity, transform;
      }

      .case-study-left-pane {
        width: 100%;
        max-height: 5000px;
      }

      .case-study-right-pane {
        width: 0;
        max-height: 0;
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateX(2rem);
        overflow: clip;
        pointer-events: none;
      }

      #case-study-page[data-panel-state='open'] .case-study-left-pane {
        width: calc(50% - 0.625rem);
      }

      #case-study-page[data-panel-state='open'] .case-study-right-pane {
        width: calc(50% - 0.625rem);
        max-height: 5000px;
        opacity: 1;
        transform: translateX(0);
        pointer-events: auto;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .case-study-shell,
      .case-study-left-pane,
      .case-study-right-pane {
        transition: none;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    function initCaseStudyPage() {
      const page = document.getElementById('case-study-page')
      const toggle = document.getElementById('case-study-toggle')
      if (!(page instanceof HTMLElement) || !(toggle instanceof HTMLButtonElement)) return
      const pageElement = page
      const toggleButton = toggle

      const mobileMedia = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 1023px)')

      function setToggleTextColor() {
        const accent = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--accent-bgc').trim()
        const match = accent.match(/(\d+)\s*,\s*(\d+)\s*,\s*(\d+)/)
        if (!match) return

        let red = parseInt(match[1], 10) / 255
        let green = parseInt(match[2], 10) / 255
        let blue = parseInt(match[3], 10) / 255

        red = red <= 0.03928 ? red / 12.92 : Math.pow((red + 0.055) / 1.055, 2.4)
        green = green <= 0.03928 ? green / 12.92 : Math.pow((green + 0.055) / 1.055, 2.4)
        blue = blue <= 0.03928 ? blue / 12.92 : Math.pow((blue + 0.055) / 1.055, 2.4)

        const luminance = 0.2126 * red + 0.7152 * green + 0.0722 * blue
        document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--case-study-toggle-text', luminance > 0.4 ? '#000' : '#fff')
      }

      function getDefaultState() {
        return 'closed'
      }

      if (!pageElement.dataset.panelState) {
        pageElement.dataset.panelState = getDefaultState()
      }

      function syncA11y() {
        const isOpen = pageElement.dataset.panelState === 'open'
        toggleButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(isOpen))
      }

      setToggleTextColor()
      syncA11y()

      toggleButton.addEventListener('click', () => {
        pageElement.dataset.panelState = pageElement.dataset.panelState === 'open' ? 'closed' : 'open'
        syncA11y()
      })
    }

    initCaseStudyPage()
    document.addEventListener('astro:after-swap', initCaseStudyPage)
  </script>
</Layout>
